# NOVVUS CRM — flujo completo demostrable (VS Code REST Client / IntelliJ HTTP)
# Requisitos: plataforma corriendo (start.bat) y módulo CRM desplegado.
# Flujo: login → roles → crear lead → convertir → mover por etapas → ganar → reporte.

@kernel = http://127.0.0.1:8000

### 0a. Registrar usuario admin (una sola vez; 409 si ya existe)
POST {{kernel}}/api/core/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "demo@novvus.dev", "password": "demo-password-123", "display_name": "Demo Admin" }

### 0b. Login
# @name login
POST {{kernel}}/api/core/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "demo@novvus.dev", "password": "demo-password-123" }

###
@token = {{login.response.body.tokens.access_token}}

### 0c. (Primera vez) Crear organización — luego re-loguear para ligar el token
POST {{kernel}}/api/core/orgs
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Novvus Demo", "slug": "novvus-demo" }

### 1. Crear el rol "Ventas" (mapeo de permisos del módulo)
# @name rolVentas
POST {{kernel}}/api/core/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Ventas", "description": "Operación diaria del CRM" }

###
@ventasId = {{rolVentas.response.body.id}}

### 1b. Permisos del rol Ventas
POST {{kernel}}/api/core/roles/{{ventasId}}/permissions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "keys": ["crm.companies.read", "crm.companies.write", "crm.contacts.read",
           "crm.contacts.write", "crm.leads.read", "crm.leads.write",
           "crm.opportunities.read", "crm.opportunities.write",
           "crm.activities.read", "crm.activities.write",
           "crm.tags.read", "crm.tags.write", "crm.pipelines.read"] }

### 2. Crear el rol "Gerente de ventas"
# @name rolGerente
POST {{kernel}}/api/core/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Gerente de ventas", "description": "Configura pipelines y ve reportes" }

###
@gerenteId = {{rolGerente.response.body.id}}

### 2b. Permisos del gerente (los de Ventas + gestión y reportes)
POST {{kernel}}/api/core/roles/{{gerenteId}}/permissions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "keys": ["crm.companies.read", "crm.companies.write", "crm.contacts.read",
           "crm.contacts.write", "crm.leads.read", "crm.leads.write",
           "crm.opportunities.read", "crm.opportunities.write",
           "crm.activities.read", "crm.activities.write",
           "crm.tags.read", "crm.tags.write", "crm.pipelines.read",
           "crm.pipelines.manage", "crm.reports.read"] }

### 3. Ver el pipeline sembrado (novvus seed) y sus etapas
GET {{kernel}}/api/crm/pipelines
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3b. Etapas
GET {{kernel}}/api/crm/stages?order_by=position&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4. Crear una empresa y su contacto
# @name empresa
POST {{kernel}}/api/crm/companies
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Novvus Aceros del Norte", "industry": "Metalurgia", "phone": "+52 81 5555 0100" }

###
@empresaId = {{empresa.response.body.id}}

### 4b. Contacto
# @name contacto
POST {{kernel}}/api/crm/contacts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Gabriela Ibarra", "email": "gibarra@acerosnorte.mx",
  "job_title": "Gerente de Compras", "company_id": "{{empresaId}}" }

###
@contactoId = {{contacto.response.body.id}}

### 5. Crear un lead (emite crm.lead.created)
# @name lead
POST {{kernel}}/api/crm/leads
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "source": "referral", "contact_id": "{{contactoId}}",
  "company_id": "{{empresaId}}", "notes": "Pidió cotización de 40 toneladas" }

###
@leadId = {{lead.response.body.id}}

### 6. Convertir el lead en oportunidad (emite crm.lead.converted)
# @name oportunidad
POST {{kernel}}/api/crm/leads/{{leadId}}/convert
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": "480000.00", "currency": "MXN", "expected_close_date": "2026-09-15" }

###
@oppId = {{oportunidad.response.body.id}}

### 6b. El lead quedó auditable: convertido y ligado a la oportunidad
GET {{kernel}}/api/crm/leads/{{leadId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7. Mover la oportunidad por etapas — obtén los stage_id del paso 3b
# (emite crm.opportunity.stage_changed)
POST {{kernel}}/api/crm/opportunities/{{oppId}}/move
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "stage_id": "PEGA-AQUI-EL-ID-DE-NEGOCIACION" }

### 8. Ganarla (emite crm.opportunity.won — Projects escuchará esto en Fase 5)
POST {{kernel}}/api/crm/opportunities/{{oppId}}/move
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "stage_id": "PEGA-AQUI-EL-ID-DE-GANADO" }

### 9. Reporte de pipeline: conteo y monto por etapa
GET {{kernel}}/api/crm/reports/pipeline
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 9b. Tasa de conversión del periodo
GET {{kernel}}/api/crm/reports/conversion?start=2026-07-01&end=2026-08-01
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Extra: actividades y etiquetas
POST {{kernel}}/api/crm/activities
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "meeting", "title": "Visita a planta", "opportunity_id": "{{oppId}}",
  "due_date": "2026-08-20T10:00:00Z" }
